{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>But you</b> — it is defiled, and its fruit, despised, you eat. The phrase is doubled. <b>And its fruit</b> — it is its bread, from the root of תנובה (produce). So too <b>ניב שפתים</b> (fruit of the lips), which is the fruit of the lips, for everything has fruit according to its nature."], :book :malachi, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Malachi -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/malachi"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:08.269499153Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}